# Placeholder — this is NOT a certificate.
#
# docker-compose.yml mounts this directory at /certs (read-only) for the `proxy`
# service, which only runs under `docker compose --profile tls`. Committing this
# file is what keeps the directory in the repo, so a standalone pantahub-base
# checkout can start the tls profile without a sibling hub tree.
#
# The hub meta-repo's `tls-local.sh on` mints the ingress certificate in here
# with mkcert:
#
#   hub.pem       leaf for hub/api/pvr/fleet.<lan-ip>.sslip.io + *.hub.localhost
#   hub-key.pem   its private key
#   rootCA.pem    mkcert's root CA, copied for containers that call the hub
#
# All three are git-ignored (see .gitignore); only this example is tracked.
# Without them Caddy has no certificate and the tls profile will not serve — run
# `tls-local.sh on` from the hub repo, or mint your own:
#
#   mkcert -cert-file .certs/hub.pem -key-file .certs/hub-key.pem <names...>
